<article class="env-lemma" id="0GXI">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/0GXI">Lemma <span data-tag="0GXI">87.7.5</span>.</a> Let $\varphi : A \to B$ be a continuous homomorphism of linearly topologized rings. If $\varphi $ is taut and $A$ is weakly pre-adic, then $B$ is weakly pre-adic. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $I \subset A$ be an ideal such that the closure $I_ n$ of $I^ n$ is open and these closures define a fundamental system of open ideals. Then the closure of $I^ nB$ is equal to the closure of $I_ nB$. Since $\varphi $ is taut, these closures are open and form a fundamental system of open ideals of $B$. Hence $B$ is weakly pre-adic. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>